        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Two rectangular pieces, \"George III and the Prince of Wales Hunting at Windsor\". Copperplate print in red (now brown) on natural tabby-woven cotton. a) shows three mounted men (Prince of Wales at left), a pack of hounds, a man holding a dead fox and another sounding a horn. b) shows a stag hunt in Windsor Great Park, with George III, the Prince of Wales, and other riding; castle upper left; part of inscription on tree trunk at lower right. Cotton browned; stains, Selvedge with two blue cords on left edge of a)."@en ;
